{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"354042e6-4fa6-43c2-81e3-607bf1588d9c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\n\nFlutter session replay in PostHog generates replays by taking screenshots of the widget tree via [`PostHogWidget`](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/installation/flutter).\n\n- In the legacy app shell ([`lib/legacy_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VKIVZw/lib/legacy_app.dart#L13-L23)), the root `MaterialApp` was wrapped inside a `PostHogWidget`.\n- In the redesigned app shell ([`lib/new_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VKIVZw/lib/new_app.dart#L23-L33)), `MaterialApp.router` was returned without `PostHogWidget`. \n- Without `PostHogWidget`, events and navigation observers still report telemetry to PostHog, but no screenshot frames are captured, leaving the session replay view empty.\n\n---\n\n### Solution\n\n1. **Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`**: Updated [`lib/new_app.dart`](file:///tmp/h-VKIVZw/lib/new_app.dart#L24-L36) to wrap `MaterialApp.router` with `PostHogWidget`, including an inline comment explaining its requirement for session replay.\n2. **Documented in `ANSWER.md`**: Detailed notes on the diagnosis and resolution have been written to [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-VKIVZw/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":78.293495,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":167106,"output_tokens":2222,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":210498,"total_tokens":169328}}}
